; serve-the-core-band.fk — the store answers first, the rented mind only on a miss.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/serve-the-core.fk
;
; The lookups are real: run against the live 875-row homecoming corpus. Row 601's question
; tokens hit; insonation's tokens (row 853, earned last night) hit; an unknown question misses.
;
; Verdict 511 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;     1  a known question is served by the body itself
;     2  its provenance is "body", not "rented"
;     4  and it costs zero rented tokens — the store answered
;     8  a word earned only last night now answers for itself: insonation
;    16  an unknown question is owed to the rented mind
;    32  which costs a rental plus a deposit — paid twice once to pay nothing forever
;    64  the rented answer is NOT trusted on arrival
;   128  and IS trusted once deposited — it stops being rented and becomes the body's own
;   256  across two known and one unknown, self-sufficiency is 6 in tenths
;
; The teaching: the inversion is a single number — hdc-locate returning nonzero. Above it sits
; the whole doctrine (subsidiarity: the body serves what it can, the rented mind only the rest)
; and the whole token economy (a hit is free, a miss is paid once and never again). Bit 64 and
; 128 are 869 source-monitoring made operational: the rented mind's fresh output is a candidate,
; never a truth, until the store has taken it — because the mind that produced it cannot tell
; its inventions from its measurements, and the store is the only thing that can.

(do
    (serve-the-core-check))
